MIT licence. The weights are downloaded the first time they are needed.

The neural key detector's weights (crates/engine/models/keynet.bin) come
from openkeyscan-analyzer, Copyright (c) 2025 Alexander Sommer, under the
MIT licence; see crates/engine/models/README.md.

USB export (crates/export) writes Pioneer's stick formats with rbox
(https://github.com/dylanljones/rbox), Copyright Dylan Jones, under the
GNU General Public License, version 3 only. Like Slint, it is one more
reason built copies are GPL-3.0. The byte layouts rbox leaves to its
caller (waveform encodings, cue colours, the analysis folder hash, MP3
frame counting, artwork thumbnails) follow Bake'n Deck
(https://github.com/M-Igashi/baken), Copyright (c) 2025 Masanari Higashi,
under the MIT licence; the files that use them say so.

The effects in crates/engine/src/effects.rs and effects/extra.rs are
openDJ's own code. Some follow published designs: Jon Dattorro's plate
reverb ("Effect Design, Part 1", JAES 1997), Andrew Simper's and Vadim
Zavalishin's zero-delay-feedback filters ("The Art of VA Filter Design"),
antiderivative anti-aliasing (Parker, Zavalishin and Le Bivic, DAFx 2016),
and the cubic interpolation, oversampling, chorus, crunch and
feedback-delay-network reverb designs of Signalsmith Audio's DSP and Basics
libraries and "Let's write a reverb" (Geraint Luff, MIT licence). No code
was copied from those libraries.

The Analog and Synthetic Groove Box kits are rendered with
mi-plaits-dsp (https://github.com/sourcebox/mi-plaits-dsp-rs), Oliver
Rockstedt's Rust port of the drum models in Mutable Instruments Plaits,
Copyright (c) Emilie Gillet, under the MIT licence.

